sequenceDiagram
    actor O as Operator / browser
    participant L as Local Setup launcher
    participant C as Owned Kubernetes cluster
    participant A as OCE Console / API
    participant K as Keycloak

    O->>L: Opt in to Kubernetes Local Setup
    L->>C: Helm pass 1: bootstrap OCE and routing CA
    L->>C: Provision Keycloak, persistent realm, TLS and DNS
    L->>K: Check discovery and client through HTTPS publication
    L->>A: Sign in as administrator, read account ID
    L->>C: Read and validate owned Envoy Service for exact egress
    L->>C: Helm pass 2: enable OIDC and recovery-only password
    L->>A: Reauthenticate for recovery, attach Alice's subject
    Note over L,A: Attachment invalidates existing OCE sessions, do not retry it.
    Note over L,A: On startup failure, attempt owned cleanup.
    Note over L,A: If cleanup is incomplete, retain state for occ dev down.
    L-->>O: Provide Console URL and browser setup instructions

    O->>A: Start browser sign-in
    A-->>O: Return authorization URL with state, PKCE and nonce
    O->>K: Follow URL and authenticate as Alice
    K-->>O: Redirect to OCE with authorization code
    O->>A: Send code and state to callback
    A->>A: Validate and consume browser-bound state
    A->>K: Exchange code with PKCE and client authentication
    K-->>A: Return tokens
    A->>K: Fetch configured JWKS
    K-->>A: Return signing keys
    A->>A: Validate token and match attached identity
    Note over A,K: Exchange/key failure or unattached identity: no OCE session.
    A-->>O: Issue host-only OCE session (eight hours)
